# .spool/parser/parser.req

feature: PARSER

requirements:
  - id: PARSER-1
    title: Req File Parsing
    description: >
      The parser must deserialize a valid .req YAML file
      into an in-memory ReqFile struct.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      YAML was chosen for its broad parser support across languages,
      unambiguous structure, and low risk of parsing edge cases.
      Ergonomics are delegated to IDE tooling rather than the file format.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: PARSER-1-1
        description: >
          Given a valid .req file,
          when the file is parsed,
          then a ReqFile struct is returned with the feature,
          and all requirements and ACs correctly populated.

      - id: PARSER-1-2
        description: >
          Given a .req file with zero requirements,
          when the file is parsed,
          then a ReqFile struct is returned with an empty
          requirements slice and no error is produced.

      - id: PARSER-1-3
        description: >
          Given a .req file with a requirement that has zero ACs,
          when the file is parsed,
          then the requirement is returned with an empty ACs slice
          and no error is produced.

      - id: PARSER-1-4
        description: >
          Given a .req file,
          when the file is parsed,
          then the SourceFile field of the returned ReqFile is
          populated with the absolute path of the parsed file.

  - id: PARSER-2
    title: ID Normalization
    description: >
      The parser must normalize all requirement and AC IDs
      to a canonical form on read, regardless of how they
      were authored.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Normalization at parse time means the rest of the system
      operates on a single canonical form and never needs to
      account for casing or zero-padding variations. This is
      the only place normalization should occur.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: PARSER-2-1
        description: >
          Given an ID authored in lowercase,
          when the file is parsed,
          then the ID is normalized to uppercase.

      - id: PARSER-2-2
        description: >
          Given an ID with leading zeros in the requirement
          or AC number segments,
          when the file is parsed,
          then the leading zeros are stripped.

      - id: PARSER-2-3
        description: >
          Given an ID that is already in canonical form,
          when the file is parsed,
          then the ID is unchanged.

  - id: PARSER-3
    title: Directory Traversal
    description: >
      The parser must recursively walk the configured reqs_dir
      and parse all discovered .req files.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Recursive traversal allows institutions to organize their
      .req files in arbitrary nested folder structures without
      any configuration beyond the root reqs_dir. The in-memory
      representation is flat regardless of nesting.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: PARSER-3-1
        description: >
          Given a reqs_dir containing .req files in arbitrarily
          nested subdirectories,
          when the directory is traversed,
          then all .req files at all nesting levels are parsed.

      - id: PARSER-3-2
        description: >
          Given a reqs_dir containing non-.req files,
          when the directory is traversed,
          then non-.req files are silently ignored.

      - id: PARSER-3-3
        description: >
          Given a reqs_dir that does not exist,
          when the directory is traversed,
          then a descriptive error is returned.

      - id: PARSER-3-4
        description: >
          Given a reqs_dir that exists but contains no .req files,
          when the directory is traversed,
          then an empty slice is returned and no error is produced.

  - id: PARSER-4
    title: Parse Error Handling
    description: >
      The parser must handle malformed .req files gracefully
      without crashing the language server.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      A file being actively edited will frequently be in an invalid
      state. The LSP must remain stable and useful during editing,
      surfacing diagnostics rather than crashing or dropping the
      entire index.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: PARSER-4-1
        description: >
          Given a .req file with invalid YAML,
          when the file is parsed,
          then an error is returned for that file and
          parsing continues for all other files.

      - id: PARSER-4-2
        description: >
          Given a .req file with a malformed ID,
          when the file is parsed,
          then an error is recorded for that requirement and
          the remaining requirements in the file are still parsed.